    "question": {
      "dom_id": "question-135491",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "In a particular town, the housekeepers use $2$ types of olive oil for preparing food: oil $A$ and oil $B.$  A study has shown that, each month \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B$, and\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these housekeepers change their preferences each month?",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the following situation for each month: \n\n- $40%$ of housekeepers who used oil $A$ swap to oil $B.$ This implies that $60%$ of them remain using oil $A.$\n\n- $30%$ of housekeepers who used oil $B$ swap to oil $A.$ This implies that $70%$ of them remain using oil $B.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Oil $A$</b></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Oil $B$</b></td> \n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">To:</td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Oil $A$</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Oil $B$</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Incorrect",
